  <h1>AI-derived Answers for the 2026 Japanese Bar Exam (Short-answer): Results Against the Official Answer Key</h1>

  <p>
    On 2026-07-24, before the official answer key existed publicly, all 113
    answer slots (Constitutional, Civil, and Criminal Law) derived by a
    multi-stage LLM verification pipeline were fixed and published with
    confidence grades and pre-designated "watch" slots. The Ministry of Justice
    released the official answer key on 2026-08-06, and every slot was matched
    against it: <strong>112 of 113 slots agreed (99.1%)</strong> — 39/40 in
    Constitutional Law, 37/37 in Civil Law, and 36/36 in Criminal Law. The
    single disagreement fell on one of the two slots designated in advance as
    most likely to diverge, all 14 low-confidence (grade B) slots matched, and
    the one slot revised by the pre-publication adversarial audit matched in its
    revised value.
  </p>

  <p>Full details are available in the <a href="/lab/r8-tanto-kekka">Japanese version</a>.</p>
